===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*speḱ-}}
From {{uder|en|la|specimen||mark, sign, example}}, from {{m|la|speciō||observe, watch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈspɛsɪmɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-specimen.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|spe|ci|men}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-specimen.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|specimina|pl2qual=extremely rare}}

# An [[individual]] [[instance]] that [[represent]]s a [[class]]; an [[example]].
#: {{ux|en|early '''specimens''' of the art of Picasso}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Bill Neal|title=Getting Away with Murder on the Texas Frontier|passage=To assure a defendant's acquittal, a lawyer usually needed only to convince the jury that the victim was a pretty sorry '''specimen''' of a human being.}}
## {{lb|en|numismatics}} A banknote printed for distribution to central banks to aid in the recognition of banknotes from a country other than their own
## {{lb|en|philately}} A postage stamp sent to postmasters and postal administrations so that they are able to identify valid stamps and to avoid forgeries
## {{lb|en|derogatory}} An [[unpleasant]] or [[contemptible]] person.
# A [[sample]], especially one used for [[diagnostic]] [[analysis]].
# {{lb|en|humorous|often preceded with “fine”}} An [[eligible]] man.

